name: Vendor context keeps draft settings, capture limits and earlier packets honest
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/vendor_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: options vendor-assessment:assess
require-live-snap: 25 Experimental | experimental-opinion
submit: logs
submit: run vendor-assessment:scope {"vendorName":"Owned vendor","profile":"operator-profile"}
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/vendor_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART set
submit: run vendor-assessment:scope {}
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/vendor_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART inspect
paste-file: @ART/scope-replay.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Profile: operator-profile | retained-profile
keys: Escape
submit: logs
submit: run vendor-assessment:attach {"source":"missing.txt","profile":"must-not-be-saved"}
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/vendor_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART failed
submit: run vendor-assessment:attach {"source":"owned-evidence.txt","title":"Owned evidence"}
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/vendor_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART attached
paste-file: @ART/capture-replay.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 text prefix only | captured-prefix
resize: 160x48
live-snap: capture-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: capture-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: capture-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: capture-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: capture-40x12
expect: 255999/256251 bytes
keys: NPage
live-snap: capture-reading-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: capture-reading-40x12-2
ask: Across six sizes, can you identify the captured prefix and omitted bytes without treating attachment completion as a complete document or repository scan?
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape
submit: logs
submit: run vendor-assessment:attach {"url":"https://example.invalid/evidence","title":"URL reference"}
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/vendor_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART referenced
paste-file: @ART/reference-replay.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 document not fetched | unfetched-reference
keys: Escape
submit: logs
submit: run vendor-assessment:prompts {"runId":"owned-packet"}
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/vendor_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART packet
submit: run vendor-assessment:scope {"clear":true}
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/vendor_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART cleared
require-live-snap: 25 draft scope cleared | cleared-draft
ask: Is clearing the current vendor draft understandable while earlier evidence receipts and generated packets remain available?
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 0 findings | auxiliary-report
expect-not: Displayed Scan: completed
keys: Home
keys: j j j
require-live-snap: 20 format json (4/6) | export-format
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 EXPORTED | exported
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/vendor_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART exported
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/capture-replay.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 text prefix only | recovered-capture
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/vendor_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart retain the earlier partial capture, cleared draft and packet without granting repository progress or starting new work?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
